<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Cold-start splash icon: the white GOV.UK wordmark centred on the GOV.UK-blue splash background.

    This is the ANDROID 12+ SYSTEM splash's icon (windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon) — the GOV.UK wordmark,
    not the app's launcher icon (@mipmap/ic_launcher). Without this set, the system splash falls back to
    showing the launcher icon (the default Android-robot icon on this app today - see the launcher-icon
    follow-up noted where this style is used), so the wordmark is required here for the cold start to show
    GOV.UK branding rather than the Android robot.

    Per the Android 12+ SplashScreen spec (https://developer.android.com/develop/ui/views/launch/splash-screen#splash-screen-dimensions),
    an icon with no icon-background set is drawn on a 288x288dp canvas, masked to an inner 192dp
    circle. The wordmark (180x34dp, preserving the 201x38 source aspect ratio) is positioned with
    explicit left/top insets rather than android:gravity="center" — gravity resolution inside a
    layer-list item was found (by on-device testing) to anchor to the start edge instead of centring,
    clipping the right side of the wordmark. Explicit insets ((288-180)/2 = 54dp left,
    (288-34)/2 = 127dp top) centre it deterministically regardless of gravity behaviour.

    @drawable/ic_govuk_logo lives in res/drawable-nodpi/ (not the unqualified res/drawable/) because
    it is a raster PNG: an unqualified drawable/ bitmap is treated by Android as an MDPI (160dpi)
    baseline asset and density-upscaled for the device's actual screen density, which compounded with
    this item's own dp sizing above to over-magnify (and blur) the wordmark on higher-density physical
    devices. drawable-nodpi/ opts the bitmap out of that automatic density scaling, leaving only this
    layer-list's explicit dp sizing in effect.

    Note: this system-splash slot is circle-masked and size-capped, so the wordmark renders smaller here
    than in the full-size in-app `SplashScreen` composable (core.root.SplashScreen) that takes over
    immediately after — that trade-off is expected and preferred over showing no GOV.UK branding at all.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:width="180dp"
        android:height="34dp"
        android:left="54dp"
        android:top="127dp"
        android:right="54dp"
        android:bottom="127dp"
        android:drawable="@drawable/ic_govuk_logo" />
</layer-list>
